{"type":"result","subtype":"success","is_error":false,"duration_ms":56750,"duration_api_ms":56722,"num_turns":8,"result":"","stop_reason":"end_turn","session_id":"e3dc1165-f5cc-46fb-8778-f7b72458ad8d","total_cost_usd":0.30983400000000005,"usage":{"input_tokens":5,"cache_creation_input_tokens":30904,"cache_read_input_tokens":119468,"output_tokens":2277,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":30904,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"","iterations":[],"speed":"standard"},"modelUsage":{"claude-opus-4-6":{"inputTokens":5,"outputTokens":2277,"cacheReadInputTokens":119468,"cacheCreationInputTokens":30904,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":0.30983400000000005,"contextWindow":200000,"maxOutputTokens":64000}},"permission_denials":[],"structured_output":{"summary":"Reviewed all four amendments against the actual source code. Three are valid improvements: the redundant Value→String→Value round-trip in post_load (confirmed at save.rs:23-24 and save.rs:114), the dead SchemaVersionMismatch variant (only occurrence is its declaration at actions.rs:73), and the silent u32 truncation bug (save.rs:120 `as u32` wraps values > u32::MAX). The fourth amendment about migration test coverage is rejected — the existing test at line 199-203 already demonstrates removing fields to simulate older saves, and the documented migration contract requires a per-bump test, making the proposed additional regression test redundant and fragile.","votes":[{"amendment_id":"fr-1-47383507","decision":"accept","rationale":"Confirmed in the code: post_load at save.rs:23 calls serde_json::to_string(&payload) on a Value, then from_json at save.rs:114 immediately calls serde_json::from_str to parse it back to Value. This is a clear redundant serialization round-trip. Adding from_value(Value) that contains the migration/deserialization logic is a clean, safe refactor that eliminates unnecessary work and simplifies the handler."},{"amendment_id":"fr-1-9fa711df","decision":"accept","rationale":"Grep confirms SchemaVersionMismatch appears only at its declaration in crates/tank_core/src/types/actions.rs:73 — no code constructs it, no match arms reference it. It is genuinely dead after the introduction of SchemaVersionTooNew/SchemaVersionTooOld. Since it's a public enum variant, clippy won't catch it. Leaving it risks future contributors reaching for the wrong, less informative variant. Safe to remove."},{"amendment_id":"fr-1-fe78d820","decision":"accept","rationale":"Confirmed at save.rs:120: `.map(|v| v as u32)` silently truncates any u64 exceeding u32::MAX. A save file with schema_version 4294967296 wraps to 0, causing the version check to emit SchemaVersionTooOld instead of the correct SchemaVersionTooNew. This is a real correctness bug — a future-version save would be misclassified. Using u32::try_from() and treating overflow as TooNew (since any version > u32::MAX certainly exceeds SCHEMA_VERSION) is the correct fix."},{"amendment_id":"fr-1-540a2c8b","decision":"reject","rationale":"While the theoretical concern is valid, the existing test suite already demonstrates the right pattern: lines 199-203 explicitly remove stability_tracker from a serialized TankState to simulate a true pre-v3 payload. The migration contract at save.rs:37-48 requires adding a migration test with each schema bump, which is where such coverage belongs — when the developer knows which field was added. A generic regression test that removes an arbitrary field is fragile, couples to current schema internals, and duplicates what the per-bump test obligation already guarantees. The existing infrastructure is adequate."}]},"fast_mode_state":"off","uuid":"a724af83-cd28-4a47-9a0a-faf6c124e71e"}
